From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:15:15 +0900
Subject: Keep an adapted singleton from being widened again under capture
 checking

Under capture checking, a reference to a value spliced by a macro as the
argument for a parameter of that value's singleton type was rejected, when
the value's own type has a capture set:

    def goImpl[T <: Path^](x: Expr[T])(using Type[T], Quotes) = '{calc[T]($x)}

    xs.map: path => go[path.type](path)

    Found:    Path^{io}
    Required: (path : Path^{io})^{path}

A type argument is boxed, so the parameter's type is `box path.type^{path}`.
The argument is adapted to it in `adapt`, which keeps a singleton as it is
when the expected type is a singleton (`noWiden`) and otherwise widens it to
its underlying type. The splice leaves the reference wrapped in an `Inlined`
node, which is adapted after the reference inside it and takes its type from
it: already adapted, `box path.type^{path}`. `noWiden` asked whether that was
a singleton without stripping its capture set, as it does for the expected
type, so the second adaptation widened it to the declared `Path^{io}`, which
is no subtype of a singleton.

The actual type is now stripped of its capture set too, so that a singleton
already adapted stays one.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: splicesingleton
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala     | 7 +++++--
 .../captures/splice-singleton-arg/Macro_1.scala          | 9 +++++++++
 .../captures/splice-singleton-arg/Test_2.scala           | 8 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Macro_1.scala
 create mode 100644 tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Test_2.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala
index 9bac259de4a6d8bc19a7efd387c5d70c8d467435..2ac2cd8c8ea01a00c3fd87fa56e910f4fb23bbf3 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/CheckCaptures.scala
@@ -2139,10 +2139,13 @@ class CheckCaptures extends Recheck, SymTransformer:
       case _ => widened
 
     /** An actual singleton type should not be widened if the expected type is a
-     *  LhsProto, or a singleton type, or a path selection with a stable value
+     *  LhsProto, or a singleton type, or a path selection with a stable value.
+     *  The actual type may itself already be adapted to a boxed `x.type^{x}`: an
+     *  `Inlined` node, as a macro splice leaves around an argument, is adapted after the
+     *  expression inside it, and takes its type from it.
      */
     private def noWiden(actual: Type, expected: Type)(using Context): Boolean =
-      actual.isSingleton
+      actual.stripCapturing.isSingleton
       && expected.match
           case expected: PathSelectionProto => !expected.selector.isOneOf(UnstableValueFlags)
           case _ => expected.stripCapturing.isSingleton || expected == LhsProto
diff --git a/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Macro_1.scala b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Macro_1.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8fcf00873a58dfb277c64b6842a0df48b40cf2b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Macro_1.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+import scala.quoted.*
+
+class Path
+
+def calc[T <: Path^](x: T): Int = 1
+
+inline def go[T <: Path^](x: T): Int = ${goImpl[T]('x)}
+
+def goImpl[T <: Path^](x: Expr[T])(using Type[T], Quotes): Expr[Int] = '{calc[T]($x)}
diff --git a/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Test_2.scala b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Test_2.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..91ff6009f6b70a53ba13d61f54aebbfbeed77a26
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos-custom-args/captures/splice-singleton-arg/Test_2.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+// A singleton argument spliced by a macro is wrapped in an `Inlined` node, which is
+// adapted after the expression inside it and takes its type, already boxed as
+// `x.type^{x}`. It must not then be widened to the declared type of `x`.
+
+def f(io: Object^, xs: List[Path^{io}]) = xs.map: path =>
+  go[path.type](path)
+
+def g(io: Object^, path: Path^{io}) = go[path.type](path)
